<section id="intro">

<h2>1. Linear Algebra kya hai?</h2>

<div class="definition">

<b>Linear Algebra</b> mathematics ki woh branch hai jo
vectors, matrices, linear equations aur linear transformations
ke saath deal karti hai.

</div>

<p>
Ab simple BCA language mein samjho.
</p>

<p>
Computer science mein bahut saara data numbers ke form mein hota hai.
Jab numbers ko systematically rows aur columns mein arrange karna hota hai,
to <b>matrix</b> ka use hota hai.
</p>

<p>
Example:
</p>

<div class="matrix">
[ 10   20   30 ]
[ 40   50   60 ]
[ 70   80   90 ]
</div>

<p>
Ye ek matrix hai.
</p>

<p>
Machine Learning, Computer Graphics, Image Processing,
Artificial Intelligence, Data Science aur Computer Vision mein
matrices bahut important hain.
</p>


<div class="important">

<b>Ek line mein:</b>

<br><br>

Linear Algebra =
Numbers/Data ko structured mathematical form mein represent karke
unpar calculations aur transformations karna.

</div>


<h3>Linear Algebra ko BCA mein kyun padhna hai?</h3>

<ul>

<li>Images ko matrices ki form mein represent kiya ja sakta hai.</li>

<li>Machine Learning models mein matrices ka use hota hai.</li>

<li>Computer graphics mein transformations matrices se hoti hain.</li>

<li>Databases aur data analysis mein matrix operations useful hain.</li>

<li>Linear equations ko solve karne ke liye matrix methods use hote hain.</li>

<li>AI algorithms mein matrix multiplication extremely important hai.</li>

</ul>

</section>


