<section id="inverse">

<h2>6. Inverse of Matrix</h2>


<h3>6.1 Inverse kya hota hai?</h3>

<div class="definition">

Matrix A ka inverse A⁻¹ woh matrix hai jiske saath multiply karne par
identity matrix milti hai.

</div>

<div class="formula">

A × A⁻¹ = I

</div>

<p>
Bilkul numbers jaisa concept:
</p>

<div class="example">

5 × 1/5 = 1

</div>

<p>
Waise:
</p>

<div class="formula">

A × A⁻¹ = I

</div>


<h3>6.2 Inverse exist kab karta hai?</h3>

<div class="important">

A⁻¹ tabhi exist karega jab:

<br><br>

det(A) ≠ 0

</div>


<h3>6.3 2×2 Matrix ka Inverse Formula</h3>

<p>
Agar:
</p>

<div class="matrix">

A =

[ a  b ]
[ c  d ]

</div>

<p>
then:
</p>

<div class="formula">

A⁻¹ =

1/(ad-bc)

×

[ d   -b ]
[ -c   a ]

</div>


<h3>6.4 Example</h3>

<div class="matrix">

A =

[ 2  3 ]
[ 1  4 ]

</div>

<p>
Step 1: determinant:
</p>

<div class="formula">

det(A)
=
(2×4)-(3×1)

<br><br>

= 8-3

<br><br>

= 5

</div>

<p>
Step 2:
</p>

<div class="matrix">

[ d  -b ]
[ -c  a ]

=

[ 4  -3 ]
[ -1  2 ]

</div>

<p>
Step 3:
</p>

<div class="formula">

A⁻¹ = 1/5

[ 4  -3 ]
[ -1  2 ]

</div>

<p>
Therefore:
</p>

<div class="matrix">

A⁻¹ =

[ 4/5   -3/5 ]
[ -1/5   2/5 ]

</div>


<h3>6.5 Inverse ko verify kaise karein?</h3>

<p>
A × A⁻¹ calculate karo.
</p>

<p>
Agar answer identity matrix aaye:
</p>

<div class="matrix">

[ 1  0 ]
[ 0  1 ]

</div>

<p>
to inverse correct hai.
</p>


<h3>6.6 Inverse ka Computing mein use</h3>

<ul>

<li>Linear equations solve karna</li>

<li>Computer graphics transformations</li>

<li>Data transformations</li>

<li>Optimization</li>

<li>Machine learning mathematics</li>

<li>Numerical analysis</li>

</ul>


<div class="tip">

Practical programming mein large matrices ka inverse
directly calculate karna hamesha best approach nahi hota.
Efficient numerical algorithms jaise matrix factorization
use ki ja sakti hain.

</div>

</section>


