<section id="equations">

<h2>7. Simultaneous Linear Equations</h2>


<h3>7.1 Simultaneous equations kya hoti hain?</h3>

<div class="definition">

Do ya do se zyada linear equations jinhe ek saath solve karna ho,
unhe simultaneous linear equations kehte hain.

</div>


<h3>7.2 Simple Example</h3>

<div class="formula">

x + y = 10

<br>

x - y = 2

</div>

<p>
Hume x aur y dono find karne hain.
</p>


<h3>7.3 Elimination Method</h3>

<p>
Equations:
</p>

<div class="formula">

x + y = 10

<br>

x - y = 2

</div>

<p>
Dono equations add:
</p>

<div class="formula">

2x = 12

</div>

<p>
Therefore:
</p>

<div class="formula">

x = 6

</div>

<p>
Ab:
</p>

<div class="formula">

x+y=10

<br>

6+y=10

<br>

y=4

</div>

<p>
Answer:
</p>

<div class="formula">

<b>x = 6, y = 4</b>

</div>


<h3>7.4 Matrix Form</h3>

<p>
Same equations:
</p>

<div class="formula">

x+y=10

<br>

x-y=2

</div>

<p>
Matrix form:
</p>

<div class="formula">

AX = B

</div>

<p>
where:
</p>

<div class="matrix">

A =

[ 1   1 ]
[ 1  -1 ]

<br><br>

X =

[ x ]
[ y ]

<br><br>

B =

[ 10 ]
[  2 ]

</div>


<p>
Therefore:
</p>

<div class="formula">

AX = B

</div>


<h3>7.5 Matrix Method</h3>

<p>
Agar A inverseable hai:
</p>

<div class="formula">

AX = B

</div>

<p>
Dono sides ko A⁻¹ se multiply:
</p>

<div class="formula">

A⁻¹AX = A⁻¹B

</div>

<p>
Because:
</p>

<div class="formula">

A⁻¹A = I

</div>

<p>
So:
</p>

<div class="formula">

IX = A⁻¹B

</div>

<p>
Therefore:
</p>

<div class="formula">

<b>X = A⁻¹B</b>

</div>


<h3>7.6 Ye concept bahut important hai</h3>

<div class="important">

Linear equations:

<br><br>

AX = B

<br><br>

Solution:

<br><br>

X = A⁻¹B

</div>

<p>
Ye matrix aur simultaneous equations ke beech ka direct connection hai.
</p>

</section>


