<section id="applications">

<h2>9. Applications of Linear Algebra in Computing</h2>


<h3>9.1 Computer Graphics</h3>

<div class="definition">

Computer graphics mein objects ko move, rotate, scale aur transform
karne ke liye matrices ka use hota hai.

</div>


<h4>Translation</h4>

<p>
Object ko ek location se doosri location move karna.
</p>


<h4>Scaling</h4>

<p>
Object ko bada ya chhota karna.
</p>

<div class="formula">

x' = sx × x

<br>

y' = sy × y

</div>


<h4>Rotation</h4>

<p>
2D rotation ke liye matrix:
</p>

<div class="matrix">

[ cosθ   -sinθ ]
[ sinθ    cosθ ]

</div>

<p>
Ye matrix point ko rotate kar sakti hai.
</p>


<h3>9.2 Image Processing</h3>

<div class="definition">

Digital image ko pixels ke matrix ke form mein represent kiya ja sakta hai.

</div>

<p>
Example grayscale image:
</p>

<div class="matrix">

[  0   50  100 ]
[ 80  120  200 ]
[ 30  180  255 ]

</div>

<p>
Har number pixel intensity represent kar sakta hai.
</p>

<p>
Generally grayscale intensity:
</p>

<ul>

<li>0 → black</li>

<li>higher value → brighter pixel</li>

<li>255 → white in a common 8-bit representation</li>

</ul>


<h3>9.3 Machine Learning</h3>

<p>
Machine learning mein data ko matrix form mein store karna common hai.
</p>

<div class="example">

Suppose 3 students aur 2 features:

<br>

Hours studied
<br>
Attendance

<br><br>

X =

[ 5   80 ]
[ 7   90 ]
[ 3   60 ]

</div>

<p>
Rows = students
</p>

<p>
Columns = features
</p>


<h3>9.4 Linear Regression</h3>

<p>
Linear regression mein:
</p>

<div class="formula">

y = mx + c

</div>

<p>
Multiple features hone par matrix notation use ki ja sakti hai.
</p>

<div class="formula">

<b>y = Xw + b</b>

</div>

<p>
where:
</p>

<ul>

<li>X = input data matrix</li>

<li>w = weights</li>

<li>b = bias</li>

