<section>

<h2>11. Important Matrix Properties</h2>

<table>

<tr>
<th>Property</th>
<th>Formula</th>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>Addition Commutative</td>
<td>A+B = B+A</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>Addition Associative</td>
<td>(A+B)+C = A+(B+C)</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>Multiplication Associative</td>
<td>(AB)C = A(BC)</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>Multiplication Distributive</td>
<td>A(B+C)=AB+AC</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>Identity</td>
<td>AI=IA=A</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>Generally Not Commutative</td>
<td>AB ≠ BA</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>Transpose</td>
<td>(AB)ᵀ=BᵀAᵀ</td>
</tr>

<tr>
<td>Inverse</td>
<td>AA⁻¹=I</td>
</tr>

</table>


<h3>Determinant Properties</h3>

<ul>

<li>det(A) = 0 → singular matrix</li>

<li>det(A) ≠ 0 → inverse exists</li>

<li>det(AB)=det(A)det(B)</li>

<li>det(Aᵀ)=det(A)</li>

</ul>

</section>


