<!-- ===================================================== -->

<section id="mistakes">

<h2>12. ⚠️ Common Mistakes</h2>


<h3>Mistake 1: Matrix Addition ke different orders</h3>

<div class="important">

2×3 matrix + 3×2 matrix directly add nahi kar sakte.

</div>


<h3>Mistake 2: Multiplication ka wrong rule</h3>

<p>
Students aksar same order ko multiplication ke liye required samajh lete hain.
</p>

<p>
Correct:
</p>

<div class="formula">

(m×n)(n×p)

</div>

<p>
Inner numbers same hone chahiye.
</p>


<h3>Mistake 3: AB = BA assume karna</h3>

<div class="important">

Generally:

AB ≠ BA

</div>


<h3>Mistake 4: Determinant rectangular matrix ka nikalna</h3>

<div class="important">

Determinant sirf square matrix ke liye hota hai.

</div>


<h3>Mistake 5: Inverse bina determinant check kiye</h3>

<p>
Pehle:
</p>

<div class="formula">

det(A) ≠ 0

</div>

<p>
check karo.
</p>


<h3>Mistake 6: 2×2 inverse formula mein signs</h3>

<p>
A:
</p>

<div class="matrix">

[ a  b ]
[ c  d ]

</div>

<p>
Inverse ke numerator mein:
</p>

<div class="matrix">

[  d  -b ]
[ -c   a ]

</div>

<div class="tip">

<b>Diagonal elements swap karo,
off-diagonal elements ke signs change karo.</b>

</div>

</section>


